{"claims":[{"claim_text":"Democratic Socialists of America recognizes the importance of the institution of collective bargaining to the betterment of the conditions of workers and their unions, regardless of sector of employment.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"Democratic Socialists of America is committed to preserving and extending democracy throughout society, including throughout the workplace, regardless of sector.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[2]},{"claim_text":"The ability to collectively bargain for better workplace conditions, salaries, and benefits improves the condition of working people not just at those workplaces, but throughout society as they are empowered to come together to better the conditions of all working men and women.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[3]},{"claim_text":"As amended per Virginia Code, Titles 40.1-52 thru 40.1-76 and 40.1-57.2, no state, county, municipal, or like governmental officer, agent or governing body has authority to recognize any labor union or other employee association as a bargaining agent of any public officers or employees, or to collectively bargain or enter into any collective bargaining contract with any such union or association or its agents with respect to any matter relating to them or their employment or service.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[4]},{"claim_text":"The law described in Virginia Code, Titles 40.1-52 thru 40.1-76 and 40.1-57.2, was passed by the Democratic-majority Virginia General Assembly and signed by Democratic Governor L. Douglas Wilder during the 1993 Legislative Session.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[4]}],"unresolved_references":[]}
```

